--TEST--
A secret argument is refused at every parameter of an extension method, one that accepts `tainted`, a sink and a `mixed` one alike, with the error a `Core` parameter gives, and inside an array at `mixed` too — `rule:security/secret-does-not-cross-an-extension`
--EXTENSION--
ledger
--FILE--
<?nvs
use Shop\Ledger;

secret string $key = "a key";

// `echoString` accepts a tainted argument. It does not accept a secret one.
string $copy = Ledger::echoString($key);

// `writeLine` is a sink, and does not accept it either.
Ledger::writeLine($key);

// `Core\Str::length` gives the same error.
uint $length = Core\Str::length($key);

// `kindOf` takes `mixed`. It does not accept a secret, alone or inside an array.
int $kind = Ledger::kindOf($key);
int $listed = Ledger::kindOf([$key]);
int $keyed = Ledger::kindOf(["key" => $key]);
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `secret string`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `secret string`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `secret string`
%A
error[E0775]: a `secret`-qualified value cannot cross a copy boundary; an extension's code reads it outside the program, %s
%A
error[E0775]: %s
%A
error[E0775]: %s
%A
error: aborting due to 6 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
